(I)--a son of Aditi; an आदित्य; married Siddhi; father of Mahiman and others;
1: भा. VI. 6. ३९; १८. 2; M. 6. 4; १५५. 7; वा. ६६. ६६; Vi. I. १५. १३१.
seized by Nandi; his eyes were pulled out by वीरभद्र (Rudra) as he made a sign with his eyes to दक्ष when he insulted शिव; शिव ordered him to see with the eye of Mitra;
2: भा. IV. 5. १७, २०; 6. ५१; 7. 3; Br. II. २४. ३३; III. 3. ६७.
to be worshipped before building a palace.
3: M. १७१. ५६; २६८. १९.

--the son of दिलीप and father of श्रुत (Suhotra वि। प्।); by penance on the banks of the Bindusaras he succeeded in bringing the Ganges; was asked how she was to dispose of the sins of men discharged into her waters; भगीरथ said that साधुस् and others among whom was Hari would take off the sins from her: was asked to pray to शिव to check her course; so he prayed to शिव and it was heard; by this he was able to shake off the sins of his ancestors;
1: भा. IX. 9. 2-१३ and १६; Br. II. १८. २५; M. १२. ४४; १५. १९; १२१. २६; वा. ८८. १६७; Vi. IV. 4. ३५-6.
a राजऋषि; went to the forest of the Gaura hills in search of गन्गा;
2: वा. ४७. २४.
his lust after more territory;
3: भा. XII. 3. १०.
after him [page२-526+ २३] गन्गा became the भागीरथी; so-called after the seventh branch of the Ganges.
4: Br. III. ५४. ४८-51; ६३. १६६-8; वा. ४७. ४०.

--(also भागवतम्) a महा- पुराण recited by कृष्ण to ब्रह्मा at the beginning of the creation;
1: भा. III. 4. १३; XII. 7. २३; Vi. III. 6. २१.
as sacred as and equal to the Veda; the sun to the darkness of Kali;
2: भा. II. 1. 8; XII. 4. ४२; I. 1. 3; 3. ४०, ४५.
a compendium of the Lord's glories; the essense of all वेदाङ्गस्, the first among the पुराणस् and just like काशि in importance;
3: Ib. II. 7. ५१; XII. 4. १५-17.
contains १८००० वेर्सेस्; abstract of the contents:--an exposition of the गायत्री and [page२-549+ ३८] the incident of the killing of वृत्रासुर; a composition of the शारस्वत Kalpa, the heyday of it;
4: Ib. II. १०. 1-१७; XII. १२. 1-४५; १३. 5, 9; M. ५३. २०-22.
fruit of studying it;
5: भा. XII. १२. ४६-68.
the पुराण Samhita1 was taught originally to नारद by the sage नारायण; नारद told it to व्यास who told it to शुक in the beginning of the द्वापर Yuga;
6: Ib. XII. 4. ४१-3; I. 7. 8; II. 1. 8.
सन्कर्षण taught it to सनत्कुमार who instructed सान्ख्यायन; he in turn imparted it to पराशर and बृहस्पति; requested by Pulastya, पराशर taught it to Maitreya;
7: Ib. III. 8. 2-9.
narrated to परीक्षित् by शुक;
8: Ib. II. 8. २८.
expounded by सूत at नैमिषालय to the sages and seers.
9: Ib. XII. 4. ४१-43.
पुराणदशलक्षणम्;
१०: Ib. II. 9. ४३.
one who makes a gift of it with a golden lion on the Full Moon day of प्रौष्तपद would reach the heaven of bliss;
११: M. ५३. २०-22.
contains १८००० stanzas.
